ys the New Orleans disaster  was unique much of the city lies below  sea level and despite years of warning  the city was woefully unprepared to  handle a breach of the levees which kept  it dry  but we are still vulnerable  see levels may rise coastlines could  erode rain patterns might change snow  packs could melt and then the waters  would rush in  you
 

